exports[`git.repo.get.sh given: [case31] a BRAND-NEW file in the worktree (untracked) when: [t2] the gitignored file is asked for by --paths directly then: read mode refuses it too — one flag, one sense 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude

🐚 git.repo.get lines
   ├─ repo: testorg/short (local)
   ├─ tree: feat/inflight
   └─ error: --paths names a gitignored file

   "scratch.local" is ignored by that repo's .gitignore.
   git.repo.get serves a repo's source, not its local scratch
   — build output, caches, and secret files stay unread.

🥥 did you know?
   ├─ see what the tree does serve
   └─ rhx git.repo.get files --in testorg/short --tree feat/inflight
"
`;

